  "notes": "Source: ATI College Catalog January 1, 2021 - December 31, 2021 (63 pp), as filed with the California Bureau for Private Postsecondary Education (BPPE); program list cross-checked against the current BPPE approved-program listing. Hand-transcribed 2026-09-30. ATI runs a modular/continuous curriculum: the catalog publishes no semester grid, so courses are grouped here into 9 sequential 'Term' blocks ordered strictly by the catalog's prerequisite chain (each term's prereqs are satisfied by earlier terms). Curriculum: Technical 72 cr (VAS 301/302, PHY 301/302, ABD 301/302, OBG 301/302 at 7.5 cr each; EXT 400 Clinical Externship 12.0 cr) + Concentration in Healthcare Administration 18 cr + General Education 30 cr = 120 cr. Caveats: (1) The catalog's course-description text lists EXT 400 as 11.5 cr, but the program curriculum table lists 12.0 cr; 12.0 is used because it reconciles with the catalog's stated totals (72+18+30=120). (2) Technical course prereqs in the catalog also name MED 101 and PHS 101, which are legacy codes not present in the current curriculum; they are documented here, not modeled. (3) ENGL 301's catalog prereq is printed as 'ENG 101' (typo for ENGL 101); not modeled as a prereq code. (4) EXT 400's catalog prereq list prints 'COMP 201' (typo for COM 201); COM 201 is placed before EXT 400 so the chain is satisfied. (5) VAS/PHY/ABD/OBG 300-level course codes and titles also appear in ATI's earlier BPPE-filed catalog edition (2020 annual report); identical codes/credits/titles.",
